      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Patients with diabetes mellitus were examined for the action of non-narcotic analgesics during oral cavity sanitation. All the drugs under study (amidopyrine, pyranal, baralgin, probon) taken per os increased the threshold of tactile painful sensitivity and the threshold of pain endurance in patients with diabetes mellitus to a greater degree than in normal subjects. No such differences were recorded after diazepam intake under the same conditions."},
